      "why": "B-flat trumpet, not a cornet: Iowa MIS trumpet, chromatic E3-D#6 in pp/mf/ff, without the cornet EQ. The Iowa recording is close-miked (harmonic centroid 3.17, 1-4 kHz +7.1 dB against 2.3 and -2 dB for trumpets heard in a room, URMP and ChoraleBricks), so a broad 2.2 kHz dip and an 8 kHz low-pass stand in for the distance: 2.77 and +3.7 dB, still the brightest brass in the band. Staccato is the sustain cut short, so both articulations have one tone.",
