  "transposition": "Informational. Rendering consumes concert-pitch MIDI exported by MuseScore; targets are keyed at sounding pitch, so no transposition is applied at playback.",
  "band_soundfont": {
    "file": "data/sounds/band/brasscribe-band.sf2",
    "about": "One SoundFont for the whole band, built by sounds/band.py. Every brass part has its own sustain preset at (bank, program) and a staccato preset at (staccato_bank = bank + 64, program). The program is the part's General MIDI program from music/src/brasscribe_music/instruments.py (gm_program), so a GM player that ignores banks still plays the right family; bank 0 of each program is the section principal (Solo Cornet, 1st Trombone, E-flat Bass, Solo Horn), which is also what a bank-less lookup finds. Percussion is bank 128 program 0 on MIDI channel 10. MusicXML numbers are 1-based: <midi-program> = program + 1, <midi-bank> = bank + 1.",
    "layering": "A part whose players use more than one target (the cornet desks) layers those targets in its preset, detuned by +-3 cents, so one MIDI channel sounds like a section; the second voice adds about 3 dB, which channel_gain_db compensates.",
    "balance": "Part balance is applied as channel volume, not inside the SoundFont: channel_gain_db = gain_db - max(gain_db) - 3 dB if layered. Measured: AVAudioUnitSampler applies almost none of an SF2 preset-level initialAttenuation and FluidSynth 0.4 of it, so a balance baked into presets would differ per engine.",
    "pop_kit_program": 1,
    "kits": "Bank 128 program 0 is the band kit: MS Basic's GM Standard kit (MIT) with the bass drums (35, 36), snares (38, 40) and crash cymbals (49, 57) replaced by VSCO 2 CE concert percussion (CC0): a muted concert bass drum, a concert snare and clash cymbals, each hit levelled to the MS Basic drum it replaces. Hi-hats, toms, side stick, ride and tambourine stay MS Basic. Bank 128 program 1 is MS Basic's Standard kit unchanged, a pop kit; nothing selects it yet (the arranger has no style signal).",
    "desk_variants": "Parts that play the same target (the three tenor horns, the two baritones, the two trombones) or the same recordings (baritone, euphonium and trombone from VSCO tenor trombone; E-flat and B-flat bass from VSCO tuba; the cornet desks) use different desk variants (players[].variant): variant v sounds, for each key, another round robin of the note or the v-th nearest other sampled note within 3 semitones. Two parts in unison then sum like two players (about +3 dB) instead of one waveform doubled (+6 dB, and a comb filter where the EQs differ). A key with no other note that close plays variant 0's sample 4 cents off. No sample is added."
  },
  "lineups": {
    "about": "Every lineup the arranger writes (music/src/brasscribe_music/instruments.py, core/brasscribe-core/src/instruments.rs) and its score part names. sounds/checks.py coverage fails if any of these parts does not resolve to its own real-sample preset. The two 'trumpet seat' lineups are the arranger's lineups with a trumpet seat, whose Trumpet part takes the lead part in place.",
