  "resolve": {
    "about": "How every player turns a score part into a band SoundFont preset. The same steps on every platform; sounds/partsound.py is the reference and sounds/partsound-vectors.json the shared test vectors. A brass part never falls back to General MIDI or a test tone: if steps 1-4 all miss, step 5 still picks a brass preset from the GM program family, and only a non-brass GM program is left unresolved (the app then says so).",
    "normalize": "lowercase; '♭' -> 'b', '♯' -> '#'; every run of whitespace (including U+00A0) -> one space; trim.",
    "steps": [
      "1. exact: the normalized name equals a normalized key of parts",
      "2. alias: the normalized name is a key of aliases",
      "3. keyword: the first keywords entry whose text is a substring of the normalized name",
      "4. instrument: the MusicXML <instrument-sound> id, or an instrument id from instruments.py, in instruments",
      "5. program: the part's 0-based General MIDI program in programs"
    ],
